          "description": "### Document name - ASR-EnableEncryptionForSNSTopic

## What does this document do?
This document enables encryption on a given Amazon SNS topic using the
[SetTopicAttributes](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sns/latest/api/API_SetTopicAttributes.html) API.

When invoked with Rollback=ROLLBACK, it restores the topic's KmsMasterKeyId to its
pre-remediation state using a snapshot stored in S3 (an originally-unencrypted topic is
restored by clearing the key).

## Input Parameters
* AutomationAssumeRole: (Required) The ARN of the role that allows Automation to perform the actions on your behalf.
* TopicArn: (Required) The ARN of the Amazon SNS Topic.
* KmsKeyArn: (Required) The ARN of AWS KMS Key.
* Rollback: (Optional) Set to ROLLBACK to execute rollback instead of remediation.
* ExecutionId: (Optional) Original SSM Automation execution ID for snapshot lookup during rollback.
* ControlExecutionId: (Optional) Level 1 (control runbook) execution ID, used as S3 snapshot key during remediation.
* SnapshotVersionId: (Optional) S3 version ID of the snapshot object, used for tamper-proof reads during rollback.
* RemediationConfigBucket: (Optional) S3 bucket name for snapshot storage.

## Output Parameters
* SnapshotRemediateOrRollback.snapshotStored
* SnapshotRemediateOrRollback.rollbackDescription
* SnapshotRemediateOrRollback.snapshotVersionId
* SnapshotRemediateOrRollback.Message
* SnapshotRemediateOrRollback.Status

## Security Standards / Controls
* AWS FSBP v1.0.0:   SNS.1
",
